## Implementation Guidelines

### Hook Development Checklist

#### Before Creating a Hook
- [ ] Hook has a single, clear responsibility
- [ ] Hook name starts with 'use' and follows naming conventions
- [ ] Hook is generic enough to be reusable
- [ ] Hook doesn't break rules of hooks

#### During Development
- [ ] All state is properly typed with TypeScript
- [ ] Error handling is comprehensive with fallbacks
- [ ] Loading states are managed consistently
- [ ] Dependencies in useEffect are complete and correct
- [ ] Expensive computations are memoized appropriately
- [ ] Cleanup functions are implemented where needed

#### Before Code Review
- [ ] Hook has proper TypeScript interfaces
- [ ] Hook is tested with unit tests
- [ ] Hook handles edge cases gracefully
- [ ] Hook follows established patterns in codebase
- [ ] Hook documentation is complete
- [ ] No console.log statements remain
- [ ] Hook performance is optimized

#### Performance Checklist
- [ ] Unnecessary re-renders are prevented
- [ ] Expensive operations are memoized
- [ ] Debouncing/throttling is used where appropriate
- [ ] Memory leaks are prevented with proper cleanup
- [ ] Caching is implemented for expensive operations

### Forbidden Patterns

#### ❌ AVOID These Anti-Patterns
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Hooks that break rules of hooks
export function useBadHook(condition: boolean) {
  if (condition) {
    const [state, setState] = useState(false); // Conditional hook
  }
  return null;
}

// ❌ WRONG - Hooks with side effects in render
export function useBadSideEffect() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  setCount(count + 1); // Side effect in render
  return count;
}

// ❌ WRONG - Hooks that don't handle cleanup
export function useBadCleanup() {
  useEffect(() => {
    const interval = setInterval(() => {
      console.log('Running...');
    }, 1000);
    // Missing cleanup
  }, []);
}

// ❌ WRONG - Hooks with missing dependencies
export function useBadDependencies(userId: string) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    fetchUser(userId).then(setUser);
  }, []); // Missing userId dependency
  
  return user;
}

// ❌ WRONG - Hooks that mutate props/state directly
export function useBadMutation(items: any[]) {
  items.push('new item'); // Mutating props
  return items;
}
```

